UPDATE decision_nodes SET data = '{"type":"info","module":5,"title":"Paramedian LP — Step-by-Step Guide","body":"[Why and when](#/node/lp-paramedian-start) | [Insertion detail and troubleshooting](#/node/lp-paramedian-insertion)\n\n**Technique per Hadzic (NYSORA).** [16]\n\n---\n\n**STEP 1: LOCATE THE TARGET INTERSPACE**\n• Straighten the patient first; correct any lean if scoliosis is present\n• Keep one hand on the **iliac crest** and your thumb on the **midline spinous processes** throughout\n• Intercristal (Tuffier) line crosses at about **L4-L5** in most, not all, patients\n• Whatever palpation suggests, stay in the **lower third of the lumbar spine**: target **L4-L5 or L5-S1**. L5-S1 is usually the largest interlaminar space\n\n---\n\n**STEP 2: MARK THE ENTRY POINT**\nFrom the center of the target interspace:\n• **2 cm lateral** to midline\n• **2 cm caudal**\n• Infiltrate local anesthetic into skin, subcutaneous tissue and paraspinal muscle along the planned track\n\n---\n\n**STEP 3: TRAJECTORY AND CONFIRMATION**\n• Direct the needle **30-45° cephalad and medially**, toward the interspace\n• **Expect no ligamentous loss of resistance.** The needle crosses soft tissue only; the first distinct give is usually the dura\n• Advance in small steps and check the hub for CSF frequently\n• Bone (lamina): withdraw to subcutaneous tissue, redirect more cephalad and walk off the superior lamina edge","citation":[12,16],"next":"lp-paramedian-insertion","images":[{"src":"images/lumbar-puncture/lp-paramedian-step1-landmarks.svg","alt":"Step 1: landmarks. Hand on iliac crest, thumb on midline; intercristal line near L4-L5; target L4-L5 or L5-S1","caption":"Step 1: Hand on the iliac crest, thumb on the midline. The intercristal line crosses near L4-L5; stay in the lower lumbar spine (L4-L5 or L5-S1)."},{"src":"images/lumbar-puncture/lp-paramedian-step2-entry.svg","alt":"Step 2: entry point 2 cm lateral and 2 cm caudal to the center of the L5-S1 interlaminar window","caption":"